WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.620
Film Courage: Why invest all that time in
short films?

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:07.020
Did you realize that you were going to work
your way up to a feature film eventually?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.180
R.L. Scott, Filmmaker: Oh yes.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.750
Feature films was always the goal from the
beginning.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:23.720
But I’ve always had a very realistic approach
to the industry.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.930
I didn’t expect to make TRANSFORMERS like
my first week out, you know what I mean?

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:35.649
I always felt like it was the craft it was
really important to study it, to understand

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:44.989
it, to be a student of film, to take my time
and sort of get as technically skilled as

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:54.539
I could through studying, through courses
or through whatever it is, not be so much

00:00:54.539 --> 00:01:03.449
in a rush to just sort of throw things out
there but really have a solid foundation and

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:08.799
a great understanding of all the different
aspects of filmmaking.

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:17.479
So most of it is to really go through the
process because you learned so much going

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:18.479
through the process.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:27.729
Like it’s one thing to have all of these
ideas but until you really go through it and

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:31.210
come out the other side like you really don’t
understand it fully.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:37.569
You don’t know what it takes to go from
script-to-screen and ll those little things

00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:40.079
in-between.

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:46.239
And so I wanted to start from a place that
I would be comfortable, to start small.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:02:08.819
Not be in a rush to branch out and make things
bigger.

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:15.680
So yes it was always in the cards to make
features but I wanted to be comfortable before

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.560
I jumped in.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.489
And then ultimately my first feature film
I produced it myself, I didn’t ask for any

00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:32.829
funding at all because I felt like I before
I could expect someone to invest in me I needed

00:02:32.829 --> 00:02:43.620
to show that I invested in myself and I needed
to show the value of my work because that’s

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:51.110
a big thing, asking someone…asking them
to take their hard-earned money and sort of

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:58.870
invest in you and just looking at it from
a realistic standpoint the question would

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:01.019
be like “Why?

00:03:01.019 --> 00:03:02.400
Why invest in you?

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.120
Can you even make this film?

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:09.400
This thing you are asking me to give you money
for can you even do it?”

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:15.480
You have to be able to show that you are able
of producing this thing that you are asking

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:25.499
people to pay you to make and so I wanted
to have a tract record of work and I wanted

00:03:25.499 --> 00:03:28.440
a body of work that they could see.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.400
Basically I wanted to take all of the “No’s”
away.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:37.930
Like any reason they would have to say no,
I wanted to take that away from them.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:48.049
And so a lot of that has to do with having
a tract record even though you haven’t had

00:03:48.049 --> 00:03:55.819
anything distributed yet or you haven’t
had any big successes there yet to at least

00:03:55.819 --> 00:04:03.499
have a body of work that can show consistent
growth in like and show the value of what

00:04:03.499 --> 00:04:07.319
you have to offer I thought was important.

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:13.889
Film Courage: When you think back to being
in Brazil and then being in South Carolina

00:04:13.889 --> 00:04:20.389
or somewhere in the South, how are you choosing
which films you watched when you were younger?

00:04:20.389 --> 00:04:25.490
Like who was influencing you, was it your
Dad or your Mom?

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:41.539
R.L.: I think it came from martial arts and
then it came from my love of storytelling.

00:04:41.539 --> 00:04:47.009
A lot of people think I only make action films
but I make every range of film I just happen

00:04:47.009 --> 00:04:54.210
to love action movies because of something
I grew up watching.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:05:02.050
But I think the martial arts was the biggest
influence but then things that had nothing

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.310
to do with action.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:15.080
I just liked really smart films, thinking
man films, film that would make you think,

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.639
maybe be a little unpredictable.

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:26.790
Maybe the approach to telling a story is unique
or sometimes it is just how you present the

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:40.750
idea, sometimes it’s the way you go about
telling the story visually, there are all

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:44.300
of these different ways.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.460
Even if you don’t have a lot of money you
can still make something unique.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:53.430
You can still do something interesting and
different.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:06:04.729
I think a lot of times people get too caught
up on the budget and they start to limit themselves

00:06:04.729 --> 00:06:05.729
based on the budget.

00:06:05.729 --> 00:06:11.430
“I don’t have enough money to do this,”
but maybe there is another way you can approach

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.919
that problem.

00:06:12.919 --> 00:06:19.169
Or maybe there is another way to approach
telling that story that could be unique that

00:06:19.169 --> 00:06:22.259
maybe doesn’t cost a lot.

00:06:22.259 --> 00:06:23.319
Maybe it’s in the way you shoot it.

00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:24.650
Maybe it’s in the way you light it.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.919
Maybe it’s in the way you edit it.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:34.789
Maybe it’s in the sound design or something
like that.

00:06:34.789 --> 00:06:43.550
Anytime I create something I never put a constraint
on it based on the dollar amount.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:48.000
I try to not think about that.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:54.259
I try to think about that in terms of how
can I approach this in an artistic way or

00:06:54.259 --> 00:06:58.430
a visually striking way or something like
that.

